// Xessly (#xs-faq): Frequently asked Straight answers. Does Xessly really fix issues without people?
---
<div class="sec" id="xs-faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><span class="eyebrow rv">Frequently asked</span><h2 class="split">Straight answers.</h2></div>
<div class="rv">
<details><summary>Does Xessly really fix issues without people?</summary><p>Yes, for every fix its agents can verify. If an agent can't prove a fix, it flags the issue with a ready draft instead of guessing.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is it an overlay?</summary><p>No. Xessly changes your actual code and content through pull requests and CMS updates.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if a fix breaks something?</summary><p>The test agent checks every change for regressions before it counts, and every change rolls back in one click.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does it guarantee WCAG or legal compliance?</summary><p>No tool can honestly guarantee that. Xessly gives you a verified record of every fix; pair it with periodic testing by disabled users and legal advice for your situation.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Xessly available now?</summary><p>Xessly is in early access. Request access and we'll be in touch.</p></details>
</div></div></div>
